    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nDNG McKenna Healy is delighted to present \"Baybush,\" 3 Hamlet Close, Balbriggan, an exceptional four-bedroom detached bungalow occupying a prime corner site with wrap-around private mature gardens. Tucked away in a peaceful enclave, this standout residence combines expansive single-story living, impressive outdoor space, and enviable proximity to the coast.\n\nStepping inside, the property features a well-proportioned layout designed for effortless family living. A welcoming hallway connects the generous principal living room, which features a fireplace, to the expansive open-plan kitchen and dining area towards the rear. The residence offers four spacious double bedrooms, including an impressive primary suite with an en-suite bathroom. A large family bathroom and a dedicated utility room off the kitchen complete the interior accommodation.\n\nOutside, the property truly sets itself apart. Enclosed by mature hedging and secure boundary walls, the wrap-around grounds offer complete privacy with extensive paved and lawned entertaining areas, alongside ample off-street parking. A key feature of \"Baybush\" is the detached garage, which has been converted into a versatile multi-use space, ideal as a home office, private gym, or entertainment room.\n\nBalbriggan has become an increasingly popular choice for families and commuters alike, thanks to its excellent transport links. The town has a mainline rail station providing regular services to Dublin city centre, while the nearby M1 motorway offers easy access to the city, Dublin Airport, and the M50. The town offers a wide range of amenities, including cafés, restaurants, local shops and larger retail options such as the Millfield Shopping Centre, which provides convenient everyday shopping. Balbriggan is particularly well regarded for its strong sense of community and excellent educational facilities. There are numerous primary and secondary schools in the area, including the highly respected Loreto Secondary School Balbriggan, which has long been recognised for its academic standards.\n\nFor those who enjoy outdoor living, Balbriggan's beautiful coastline and beaches offer wonderful opportunities for walking, swimming and relaxation, while a variety of local sports clubs, parks and recreational facilities contribute to the town's active lifestyle. Combining coastal charm, community spirit and superb connectivity, Balbriggan continues to grow in popularity as a place to live while remaining within comfortable commuting distance of Dublin city."
      },
